// @run
// @log 7
// The BOUNDARY of `type-param-list-field.vl`, and the measurement that located it: a
// generic alias whose body arrays its type parameter is an emit error with NO
// application anywhere in the program. `collectA` walks every `TypeRef` in the arena,
// reachable or not, so the alias DECLARATION's own `T[]` is what reached
// `checkArrName` — which is why varying the element type, the argument count and the
// instantiation count all read the same cell.
//
// Also the regression guard for the skip: a program that mints no instance must still
// compile, exactly as the never-applied recursive alias next door does.
type Box<T> = { v: T[] }

const n = 7
print(n)
